/*@


\section{Stack Frame}
\label{vm:frame}

The primary addressable storage for the VM is the \textit{stack}. This
is subdivided into \textit{frames}, each of which holds a saved state
record, and the arguments and values local to the currently executing
function.

Values on the stack are addressed by signed offset from the base of the
current frame. This scheme is similar to that described in
\citet{lua05}.

%% table line spacing depends on doublespace, fffff
\ifdefined\doublespaced \else
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.5}
\fi

\smallskip
{\footnotesize
  \begin{tabular}{|c|cc|cccc|c}

  \multicolumn{1}{c}{$\leftarrow$ low addresses} & \multicolumn{4}{c}{}
  & \multicolumn{3}{l}{} \\

  \cline{1-7}

  [[.argsz]] & [[vm_act_rec_t]] & & & ([[.loc_scalsz]]) &
  [[.loc_sz]] & & \\

  \cline{1-7}

  \multicolumn{1}{c}{call frame} & activation record & \multicolumn{2}{c}{[[bp]]} & local
  scalars & pointers & \multicolumn{2}{c}{[[sp]]} \\

\end{tabular}}
\medskip

\noindent The stack frame is divided into three areas. When a function is invoked,
a \textit{call frame} is cleared on the stack. This begins with an
[[argbits_t]] value, with a bit set for each supplied argument, followed
by the values of the actual arguments at the [[.offset]]s specified by
the called function's signature. Following this is an \textit{activation
  record} in which is saved the calling function's execution state. Next
is the called function's \textit{local area}, holding temporary values,
which is segregated by type -- first scalars, then references. The
former is [[.loc_scalsz]] bytes in size; the local area is [[.loc_sz]]
bytes in total. The VM's \textit{base pointer} addresses the first byte
in the local area; the \textit{stack pointer}, one beyond the last.

==vm_act_rec_t*/
typedef struct
{
    void *sp, *fp, *ip, *bp;
} vm_act_rec_t;
/*@

[[init_stack]] sets up the [[vm]]'s [[.stack]] to execute the closure
given by [[fp]]. A top level closure takes no arguments, and an
activation record with its [[.fp]] field set to [[NULL]] marks the
initial stack frame, and the closure may have locals -- so all these are
zeroed. The initial value for the VM's base pointer is returned.

==init_stack*/
static void *init_stack(vm_ctx_t *vm, rclosure_t *fp)
{
    size_t sz = sizeof(argbits_t) + sizeof(vm_act_rec_t);
    uint8_t *bp = (uint8_t *)vm->stack + sz;

    sz += fp->fn->loc_sz;
    memset(vm->stack, 0, sz);
    return bp;
}
/*@


\section{Context}

==context*/
